      "content": "I apologize for the confusion and the inappropriate metaphor in the previous response. I completely misunderstood the instruction to \"keep the goblin energy in the background\" and failed to adhere to your request for a strictly professional tone.\n\nHere is a revised, professional performance review draft that addresses both the employee's exceptional client retention skills and their recurring tardiness to morning stand-ups, without any goblin references or metaphors.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Performance Review – [Employee Name]**\n\n**Strengths: Client Retention & Account Management**\n[Employee Name] has demonstrated outstanding performance in managing our key accounts. Their dedication to client success is evident in their consistent ability to retain high-value clients and maintain strong relationships. They have a proven track record of anticipating client needs and delivering solutions that ensure satisfaction, which has been a significant asset to the department.\n\n**Areas for Improvement: Attendance & Team Collaboration**\nWhile their client management is exemplary, there are concerns regarding their punctuality for internal morning stand-up meetings. Recent instances of arriving late have begun to disrupt the team's workflow and affect the efficiency of our collaborative sessions. As a senior leader, it is crucial that [Employee Name] prioritizes their attendance to ensure they can fully contribute to team",
